From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] packaging: recognise riscv64 in the platform-tag validator

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted yet: enola-labs/enola's own release.yml builds no riscv64 wheel, so the regex change cannot be exercised by upstream's own CI; opening it needs a maintainer discussion of adding a riscv64 build leg first]

build_wheel.py's PLATFORM_TAG_RE checks the shape of --platform-tag before
writing the wheel, and its manylinux alternative only recognises aarch64
and x86_64. A tag of manylinux_2_39_riscv64, built from a real riscv64
enola binary, is rejected by this check before any wheel is written,
even though the script otherwise makes no architecture assumption.

Add riscv64 to the manylinux alternative, matching the aarch64/x86_64
spelling already there. musllinux is left unchanged: this port does not
build a musl wheel.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 packaging/pypi/build_wheel.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packaging/pypi/build_wheel.py b/packaging/pypi/build_wheel.py
index 4dd271d..1295289 100755
--- a/packaging/pypi/build_wheel.py
+++ b/packaging/pypi/build_wheel.py
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ HOMEPAGE = "https://github.com/enola-labs/enola"
 PLATFORM_TAG_RE = re.compile(
     r"^(?:"
     r"macosx_\d{1,2}_\d{1,2}_(?:arm64|x86_64)"
-    r"|manylinux_2_\d{1,2}_(?:aarch64|x86_64)"
+    r"|manylinux_2_\d{1,2}_(?:aarch64|riscv64|x86_64)"
     # The legacy alias for manylinux_2_17. Not redundant: pip only learned the
     # PEP 600 manylinux_<major>_<minor> spelling in 20.3, and RHEL and Rocky 8
     # ship pip 20.2.4, so a wheel tagged only manylinux_2_17 is invisible to
